{
    "background_story": "Emelia was a bright-eyed and cheerful high school student with a passion for music. Every winter, she would gather her friends and form a caroling group to spread holiday cheer throughout their small town. With Emelia's powerful voice leading the way, they would sing classic Christmas tunes at local nursing homes, hospitals, and even on street corners. Her love for caroling was contagious, and soon the group grew to include students from all walks of life. Emelia's kindness and dedication inspired others to join in, and their caroling sessions became a beloved town tradition. As the years passed, Emelia's group continued to grow, and their joyful voices could be heard ringing out across the snowy streets, bringing warmth and happiness to all who listened.",
